ts name to CoreWeave, Inc. in December 2019. CoreWeave, Inc. was incorporated in 2017 and is based in Livingston, New Jersey.","ceo_bio":"Mr. Michael N. Intrator | Co-founder, President, CEO & Chairman | Age 55 | Compensation: $3.5M (FY2025)","culture_narrative":"Employs approximately 2K people. Revenue per employee of $2.3M ranks in the top quartile among Technology peers. Stock-based compensation of $288K per employee reflects an ownership culture. CEO compensation is 1\u00d7 revenue per employee (modest relative to workforce productivity). Governance score flags elevated compensation governance risk (7/10).","financial_summary":["CoreWeave, Inc. is a large-cap technology business with a $25.6B market cap on $5.1B of annual revenue.","Returns on capital run at -0% against a 8% cost of capital, which means the business is destroying value with every dollar it reinvests.","The company is burning through $7.3B of cash, and without positive owner earnings any valuation rests on hope rather than evidence.","Accruals are elevated at -8.6% of assets, and Sloan showed firms building earnings through accruals rather than cash systematically underperform.","On the balance sheet, debt is heavy at 7.6\u00d7 net debt/EBITDA, and leverage like that is what turns a bad year into a permanent loss, and thin -0.0\u00d7 interest coverage leaves no room for a bad year.","Shareholder yield is only 0.0%, a thin return of capital, and stock-based comp at 12% of revenue is silent dilution an owner has to account for, and insiders hold 19% of the shares, so management thinks like owners because it is one \u2014 the strongest alignment there is, and profit capture is only 0.0\u00d7 the fair share, suggesting no structural edge inside its industry."],"sector_headwinds":[{"text":"Altman Z in the distress zone (0.1) \u2014 the kind of balance-sheet risk that can make a loss permanent","sev":"red","cat":"quality"},{"text":"Very elevated short interest (22.4% of float) \u2014 sophisticated money is betting against the business","sev":"red","cat":"sentiment"},{"text":"News sentiment sharply negative (-0.37) across 12 recent articles \u2014 the narrative has turned","sev":"red","cat":"news"},{"text":"Fragmented industry with below-average profit capture \u2014 no moat to protect margins","sev":"amber","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Insiders are net sellers (100% sell ratio, net $75.0M) \u2014 the people closest to the business are reducing their personal stake","sev":"amber","cat":"insider"},{"text":"Carries more leverage than most Technology peers \u2014 a smaller cushion for the inevitable bad year","sev":"amber","cat":"balance_sheet"},{"text":"Technology sector lagging the market significantly, underperforming by 7% over 3 months","sev":"amber","cat":"sector"},{"text":"Elevated sector volatility (35% annualized) adds uncertainty","sev":"amber","cat":"sector"},{"text":"Above-average market volatility (VIX 26)","sev":"amber","cat":"macro"},{"text":"Cybersecurity liability and talent cost inflation \u2014 a single breach can erase years of goodwill, and the war for engineering talent compresses margins even at scale.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"}],"sector_tailwinds":["Trading near the bottom of its 52-week range \u2014 the market is offering a discount","Founder-led \u2014 owner alignment that often matters more than any incentive plan","Minimal goodwill on the balance sheet \u2014 low impairment risk"],"news_headlines":[{"title":"CoreWeave (NASDAQ:CRWV) Stock Price Up 6.3% \u2013 Time to Buy?","source":"thelincolnianonline.com","link":"https://www.thelincolnianonline.com/2026/11/06/coreweave-nasdaqcrwv-stock-price-up-6-3-time-to-buy.html","date":"2026-11-06","timestamp":1794003688.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.881,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":["m_and_a"]},{"title":"AI Cloud Crash Puts CoreWeave and Nebius on Sale. Their Next Reports Decide What Happens Next","source":"aol.com","link":"https://www.aol.com/articles/ai-cloud-crash-puts-coreweave-163800